content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Research": {
      "objects": [
        "Fiscal Data",
        "File Format",
        "Visibility Status",
        "Geographic Information",
        "Contextual Information",
        "Dataset",
        "Title",
        "Metadata",
        "Population",
        "Area",
        "GDP",
        "Fiscal Data Insight",
        "Data Consumer",
        "Dataset Request"
      ]
    },
    "Publishing": {
      "objects": [
        "Publisher",
        "Fiscal Data",
        "File Format",
        "Visibility Status",
        "Geographic Information",
        "Contextual Information",
        "Dataset",
        "Title",
        "Metadata",
        "Population",
        "Area",
        "GDP"
      ]
    },
    "Administration": {
      "objects": [
        "Platform",
        "Platform Policies",
        "User Roles",
        "Platform Administrator",
        "Dataset Request"
      ]
    },
    "subdomain connections": [
      "Research--Publishing",
      "Administration--Publishing",
      "Administration--Research"
    ]
  }
}
```
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Publisher",
      "desc": "A user or organization responsible for publishing and managing fiscal datasets on the platform"
    },
    {
      "name": "Fiscal Data",
      "desc": "Structured financial information about public spending, revenues, or budgets",
      "attributes": [
        "File Format",
        "Visibility Status",
        "Geographic Information",
        "Contextual Information",
        "Dataset"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "File Format",
      "desc": "The technical format used for importing or publishing fiscal data"
    },
    {
      "name": "Visibility Status",
      "desc": "Indicates who can access or view the data"
    },
    {
      "name": "Geographic Information",
      "desc": "Spatial or regional data linked to fiscal information"
    },
    {
      "name": "Contextual Information",
      "desc": "Supplementary data that provides interpretive context for fiscal figures"
    },
    {
      "name": "Dataset",
      "desc": "A collection of fiscal data records",
      "attributes": [
        "Title",
        "Metadata",
        "Population",
        "Area",
        "GDP"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Fiscal Data Insight",
      "desc": "An analytical view or visualization derived from fiscal datasets"
    },
    {
      "name": "Platform Administrator",
      "desc": "A user with elevated privileges who oversees platform activity"
    },
    {
      "name": "Platform",
      "desc": "The digital environment that hosts fiscal data publication, exploration, and management",
      "attributes": [
        "Platform Policies"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Dataset Request",
      "desc": "A request submitted by a data consumer to access, modify, or publish a dataset, requiring administrator review"
    },
    {
      "name": "User Roles",
      "desc": "The defined roles within the platform with specific permissions and access levels"
    },
    {
      "name": "Data Consumer",
      "desc": "A user who accesses fiscal datasets for analysis and reporting."
    }
  ]
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- Identify cases, where an object does not have a unified meaning across all bounded contexts and suggest a name change.
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```
